## First-time setup (once per machine)

```bash
git config --global user.name  "Your Name"
git config --global user.email "you@company.com"
git config --global core.editor "vim"
git config --global credential.helper store
git config --global pull.rebase true      # cleaner history on pull
```

---

## Clone the project repo

```bash
git clone git@github.com:your-org/asic-dv-project.git
cd asic-dv-project
git status
```

---

## Daily loop

```bash
git pull origin main                          # 1. always start here
# ... edit your files ...
git add tb/sequences/your_file.sv             # 2. stage specific file
git add -A                                    # 2. or stage everything
git status                                    # 3. confirm staging
git commit -m "feat(axi): short description"  # 4. commit with clear message
git push origin your-branch-name              # 5. push to GitHub
```

