## Branches

```bash
# Create and switch to a new branch
git checkout -b feat/rs-axi-stress-seq

# List all branches (including remote)
git branch -a

# Switch between existing branches
git checkout main

# Keep your branch up to date with main
git fetch origin
git rebase origin/main

# Push branch + open PR (GitHub prints URL)
git push origin feat/rs-axi-stress-seq

# Delete local branch (after merge)
git branch -d feat/rs-axi-stress-seq

# Delete remote branch
git push origin --delete feat/rs-axi-stress-seq
```

### Branch naming

| Prefix      | Use for                                  |
|-------------|------------------------------------------|
| `feat/`     | New test, sequence, or feature           |
| `fix/`      | Bug fix in testbench or scoreboard       |
| `cov/`      | Functional coverage model work           |
| `refactor/` | Code cleanup, no behaviour change        |
| `chore/`    | Build, CI, config changes                |

Pattern: `type/your-initials-short-description`
Example: `feat/rs-axi-back2back-write`

