## Undo & recover

| Situation | Safe command |
|-----------|-------------|
| Discard unstaged edits to a file | `git restore <file>` |
| Unstage a file (keep edits) | `git restore --staged <file>` |
| Fix last commit message (not pushed) | `git commit --amend -m "new message"` |
| Add missed file to last commit (not pushed) | `git add <file> && git commit --amend --no-edit` |
| Undo last commit, keep changes staged | `git reset --soft HEAD~1` |
| Undo last commit, keep changes unstaged | `git reset HEAD~1` |
| Safely undo a pushed/merged commit | `git revert <hash>` |
| Save WIP before switching branch | `git stash push -m "wip: description"` |
| Restore WIP | `git stash pop` |
| Find a "lost" commit | `git reflog` |

> **Rule:** Use `git revert` on shared/pushed branches. Use `git reset` only on local unpushed commits.

