## Team ops

```bash
# Who last changed each line?
git blame tb/scoreboard/axi_sb.sv
git blame -L 45,60 tb/scoreboard/axi_sb.sv   # specific lines only

# Find which commit broke a regression (binary search)
git bisect start
git bisect bad                    # current HEAD is broken
git bisect good v2.4-release      # last known good tag or hash
# run regression, then:  git bisect bad  OR  git bisect good
# repeat ~6 times — git announces the first bad commit
git bisect reset                  # return to original branch

# Apply a single commit from another branch
git cherry-pick <commit-hash>
git cherry-pick --continue        # after resolving any conflict

# Tag a tapeout or release milestone
git tag -a v1.0-tapeout-freeze -m "Regression at 98.3% — tapeout freeze"
git push origin --tags

# Search commit history
git log --grep="scoreboard" --oneline
git log --author="R. Sharma" --oneline
git log --oneline -- tb/scoreboard/axi_sb.sv
git log --oneline --graph --all --decorate   # visual branch graph
```

